    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you're saying about apophenia and traffic patterns, but it's hard to ignore when the timing gets so precise. like, if it's just random volume, why would it consistently lean towards longer greens on my high-stakes days and shorter ones on my chill days? it's like the city's infrastructure is sync'd to my calendar. \n\nis there a way to look at this more objectively? like, if we assume for a second there *is* a logic or a sequence to the timing, how would a system like that even work? like what would a \"go\" signal vs a \"wait\" signal look like in a data set? i'm just trying to understand the mechanics of what i'm seeing.",
